{"data": [{"author_id": "423769635", "created_at": "2026-11-11T20:38:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120617063412900045"], "id": "2120617063412900045", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2173, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "China’s earnings growth has fallen short of analyst expectations for nine years in a row.\n\nSource: Goldman Sachs via @MikeZaccardi https://t.co/pWW8DafMyB", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2120617063412900045"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-11-11T19:49:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120604833187049756"], "id": "2120604833187049756", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 971, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Not stimulus!\nhttps://t.co/cU3nqdmApj", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2120604833187049756"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-11T19:07:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120594341173580156"], "id": "2120594341173580156", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 11667, "like_count": 32, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120540967010750787", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I feel like the Wikipedia editors aren't doing the readers any analytical favors here by using these two maps. Total voteshare for Dems grew significantly in 2026. The fact that the Democrats won more NC Congressional seats isn't, in and of itself, evidence of a dummmymander. https://t.co/VXja1drCso", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120594341173580156"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-11T18:42:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120587929760530735"], "id": "2120587929760530735", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1333, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Future news headline about EA? https://t.co/spC22lBNha", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120587929760530735"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-11T18:33:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120585815029903440"], "id": "2120585815029903440", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11002, "like_count": 22, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "Best 3 days for $SMH since mid-June", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120585815029903440"}, {"author_id": "961132338", "created_at": "2026-11-11T18:32:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120585386871406675"], "id": "2120585386871406675", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2120, "like_count": 20, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120584911031542221", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Old enough to remember when Spain's big problem was that house prices were too low... https://t.co/mBQnnbW6sD", "url": "https://x.com/M_C_Klein/status/2120585386871406675"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-11T18:26:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120584064101130302"], "id": "2120584064101130302", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 14236, "like_count": 74, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "$CRWV is up 27%", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120584064101130302"}, {"author_id": "423769635", "created_at": "2026-11-11T18:00:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120577329483383081"], "id": "2120577329483383081", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 4027, "like_count": 24, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Credit cards originated during 2020–22 experienced a sharp rise in serious delinquencies in 2023–24, potentially reflecting weaker borrower credit quality at origination. However, their contribution to new delinquencies has since diminished.\n\nSource: https://t.co/j0hc7f6R7y https://t.co/cK10EemMvm", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2120577329483383081"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-11-11T17:59:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120577165242884542"], "id": "2120577165242884542", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1100, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "WuXi AppTec Removed From Pentagon’s List of Chinese Military Companies\nhttps://t.co/xECV14vowH", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2120577165242884542"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-11T17:46:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120573791231430961"], "id": "2120573791231430961", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2983, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120557938292969773", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Hope gasparino wrong that Jensen huang will have to resign. Grim segment https://t.co/xCWZdnizZu", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2120573791231430961"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-11-11T17:25:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120568607361098039"], "id": "2120568607361098039", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 6397, "like_count": 30, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "Xinhua: “China will strive to build an accounting system with Chinese characteristics that is internationally leading in 2026-30.”\nhttps://t.co/lTAMKW2p1h", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2120568607361098039"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-11-11T17:18:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120566766598496482"], "id": "2120566766598496482", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 57, "impression_count": 12546, "like_count": 191, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 36}, "text": "Bloomberg: “Russia has effectively abandoned attempts to replace the dollar with China’s yuan under the pressure of US secondary sanctions, underlining the difficulties facing other nations looking for an alternative global currency.”\n\nAs I’ve long explained, surplus countries", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2120566766598496482"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:53:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120560637495644490"], "id": "2120560637495644490", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 2630, "like_count": 33, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "Indeed job postings:\n\n1/ The surge in US software development postings continues - we're at the highest level in over 3 years, though still about a year away at current growth rates (~24% Y/Y) from the pre-pandemic levels. https://t.co/Fu7Sx0UBz0", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120560637495644490"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:38:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120556908734025806"], "id": "2120556908734025806", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1157, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"When world leaders fly into Shenzhen next wk, they may catch a glimpse of #China's vision for the future of global trade: a high-tech port humming w/next-gen hardware &amp; software...The Mawan Terminal—complete w/its driverless trucks, remote-controlled cranes &amp; #AI-powered", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2120556908734025806"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-11T16:19:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120551997531414835"], "id": "2120551997531414835", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 4583, "like_count": 12, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "1/ Since real wage growth discourse is back, a reminder: using headline inflation introduces a lot of noise.\n\nIt's fine for some uses (what's happening very recently) but less useful if you're interested in trends.\n\nMuch of the recent real wage growth weakening won't persist. https://t.co/fMWzpzprHN", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120551997531414835"}, {"author_id": "423769635", "created_at": "2026-11-11T15:55:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120545875130769452"], "id": "2120545875130769452", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 18, "impression_count": 6356, "like_count": 35, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 9}, "text": "Since 2000, stocks have returned an average of 7.7% annually, but missing the 10 best trading days each year would have turned that gain into a 15.4% average annual loss, highlighting the risks of market timing.\n\nSource: @RyanDetrick https://t.co/bDYgpbq3fk", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2120545875130769452"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-11T15:50:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120539671335780835", "2120544597961240583"], "id": "2120544597961240583", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 3663, "like_count": 39, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120535941043646555", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Bessent throwing lutnick under the bus? https://t.co/8TGXdjo5Ki", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2120544597961240583"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-11T15:30:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120539671335780835", "2120544597961240583"], "id": "2120539671335780835", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 1589, "like_count": 15, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120535941043646555", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Bessent throwing nutlick under the bus? https://t.co/8TGXdjnxUK", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2120539671335780835"}, {"author_id": "3039504459", "created_at": "2026-11-11T15:15:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120535814035603590"], "id": "2120535814035603590", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 13, "impression_count": 2435, "like_count": 38, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 12}, "text": "High-speed cameras capture a brief temperature dip in a vertically shaken granular fluid during its initial relaxation. Simulations and kinetic theory link this Kovacs memory effect to coupling between horizontal and vertical temperatures.\n\nRead more: https://t.co/mPUwolPfmD https://t.co/sRYbRr9ExS", "url": "https://x.com/PhysRevLett/status/2120535814035603590"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-11T15:12:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120535260131889273"], "id": "2120535260131889273", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1815, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119988541317140724", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Am I weird for thinking that this visualization, while visually striking, is clunky at info transmission?\n\nThe counties should be sized by vote margin imho https://t.co/sRQBevmgi6", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120535260131889273"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-11T13:51:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120514689805295657"], "id": "2120514689805295657", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 19317, "like_count": 43, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 9}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120161377247469967", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "This chart matches Fedlock, which also identifies yesterday's speech as Waller's most hawkish since 2023. There's no \"ground truth\" with measuring sentiment like this, but it's not to see my approach roughly align with other, existing techniques. https://t.co/zVh6WKpRAj https://t.co/iet4mpU0Rb https://t.co/CZnm3qKXTi", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120514689805295657"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-11T13:18:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120506383678509186"], "id": "2120506383678509186", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 20, "impression_count": 74226, "like_count": 433, "quote_count": 14, "reply_count": 28, "retweet_count": 25}, "text": "*ANTHROPIC MEGA-IPO IS SAID TO BE MULTIPLE TIMES OVERSUBSCRIBED", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120506383678509186"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-11T13:10:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120504367652491396"], "id": "2120504367652491396", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 28, "impression_count": 16921, "like_count": 51, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 9}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120360815932944838", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "“A person granted anonymity to discuss Nvidia’s strategy said the company is moving away from the “aggressive elements of the approach” that it once took in Washington. The person attributed the shift to new leadership in its federal affairs team, after Nvidia hired Bruce https://t.co/7Rhe0WswrN", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2120504367652491396"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-11T12:45:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120498093586325906"], "id": "2120498093586325906", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2822, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120430280205115441", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Sucks for US soccer https://t.co/zjALElcirR", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2120498093586325906"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-11-11T12:34:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120495431809700244"], "id": "2120495431809700244", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 37996, "like_count": 1364, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 56, "retweet_count": 31}, "text": "Honoring my Dad Ralph on #VeteransDay who proudly served in the Air Force during the Korean War … this is me with my parents